learning_objective:
Upon successful completion of the course, participants will be able to:
1. distinguish between finite-population and classical statistical inference;
2. compare and evaluate the designs: simple random, stratified, and cluster sampling designs with respect to
their their strengths, limitations, and fields of application;
3. use R to analyze sample survey data;
4. identify and address issues related to missing and erroneous data;
5. critically assess the quality of survey estimates within the total survey error framework.

content:
Key topics include:
- Linear programming and polyhedra;
- Flows and cuts;
- Combinatorial optimization problems and polyhedral techniques;
- Equivalence between optimization and separation.

